>Ok, so what exactly is the mirror trick?

Well I know it can sometimes annoy people to refer to a trick or feature
of the game without explanation but since I posted this only a few
months ago I didn't bother rehashing it. Anyway....

SPOILERS!

When you are blind you can apply a mirror to yourself. Usually you get
a message "You can't see your ugly face". Sometimes however you get a 
message which hints roughly how many levels below you the Wizard is
(or Medusa if you haven't killed her yet).
If the Wizard is ten or less levels down you get told he lives "below
you", but if it is more than ten levels it is "FAR below you".
So you walk back up through the dungeon from the castle, applying
your mirror at each level. If the wizard is ten or less levels below
the castle, at some level the message will change from "below" to "far
below". So you know that the wizard is now 11 levels down from your
current level. (Of course, if the wizard is more than 10 levels below
the castle you always get the "far below" message and you just have to
teleport to level 50). So in the above game, the castle was at level 28
and the wizard was "below" me on levels 27 and 26. On level 25, he was
"far below". 25 + 11 = 36.
Once you have pinpointed on what level he resides, just head for the
nearest level teleporter, and GOOD LUCK!

